      "id": "002",
      "headline": "Scientist Trent Lent Invents Sentient Tent That Rents Itself Out",
      "summary": "The tent reportedly charges $50 a night and refuses to host anyone who snores.",
      "fullBody": "Dr. Trent Lent, a biologist from Kent, spent ten years developing the world's first self-aware tent. 'I wanted to revolutionize camping,' Lent explained, 'but now it has opinions about polyester blends.' The tent, named 'Tentacle Tent,' has already listed itself on three rental platforms and is currently suing a camper for leaving crumbs inside. Legal experts are tentatively watching the case unfold.",
