      "id": "003",
      "headline": "Mayor Fay Gray Bans Gray Days, Declares Every Day Must Be 'Ray Day'",
      "summary": "Citizens required to wear sunglasses indoors; meteorologists are in disarray.",
      "fullBody": "Mayor Fay Gray of Grayville, Indiana, has issued an executive order banning overcast skies. 'Gray days make people feel gray,' Gray declared from a podium bathed in artificial sunlight. The decree mandates that every day be renamed 'Ray Day,' requiring citizens to smile at strangers and carry pocket flashlights. Local weatherman Jay Kay resigned in protest, stating, 'You can't just ban clouds. That's not how atmosphere works.' Gray responded by appointing a 'Chief Ray Officer' to patrol the skies with mirrors.",
      "category": "politics",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-07-06/003.jpg",
