      "id": "006",
      "headline": "Cat Pat Mat Battles Rat Tat Sat in Epic Backyard Chat spat",
      "summary": "The confrontation lasted three hours; neither feline nor rodent would scat.",
      "fullBody": "In the suburbs of Flat Hat, a territorial dispute between Pat Mat, a tabby cat, and Tat Sat, a surprisingly eloquent rat, escalated into a full-blown argument. Witnesses report the two exchanged heated meows and squeaks for three hours before a mediator named Nat Bat intervened. 'They were just venting about property lines,' Bat explained. The conflict was resolved when both parties agreed to share a saucer of milk at twilight. Local dogs are reportedly 'deeply disappointed' by the peaceful resolution.",
      "category": "animals",
