      "id": "007",
      "headline": "Artist Bart Dart Farts His Way to Modern Art Stardom with 'Heart Chart'",
      "summary": "The piece sold for $2 million; critics call it 'a breath of fresh air.'",
      "fullBody": "Bart Dart, a controversial performance artist from Dartmouth, has shattered auction records with 'Heart Chart,' a multimedia installation combining flatulence and cardiac monitoring. 'Each toot is mapped to my heartbeat,' Dart explained, wearing a tuxedo made of smart fabric. The piece, which sold for $2 million to an anonymous collector, has divided the art world. 'It's visceral, it's human, it's slightly nauseating,' said critic Marta Carta. Dart is already working on a sequel, 'Smart Fart,' which will incorporate AI-generated harmonies.",
