      "id": "008",
      "headline": "Pilot Wyatt Knight Fights Plight of Flight Delight with Kite-Powered Plane",
      "summary": "The aircraft runs on wind and whimsy; TSA is baffled.",
      "fullBody": "Captain Wyatt Knight, a pilot with a penchant for the poetic, has unveiled a commercial airliner powered entirely by giant kites. 'Why fight the wind when you can invite it?' Knight asked while untangling a string from a baggage carousel. The maiden flight from Portland to Portland (a different one) took 14 hours but used zero fuel. Passengers described the experience as 'surprisingly serene, except for the screaming when a kite dipped.' The FAA is reviewing the design while eating anxiety medication.",
