      "id": "011",
      "headline": "Singer Bing King Sings Ring Song in Spring, Brings Zing to Everything",
      "summary": "The concert was so lively that even the chairs danced.",
      "fullBody": "Bing King, the self-proclaimed 'King of Bing,' performed his hit 'Ring Song' at the Spring Fling in Zing, Kansas. The concert was so energetic that witnesses report folding chairs spontaneously line-dancing and a tuba player ascending to a higher plane of existence. 'I just wanted to sing about jewelry,' King said, adjusting his diamond-encrusted crown. The event raised $50,000 for the local library, which plans to install a 'Bing Wing' dedicated to books that rhyme. Attendees are still humming the tune six days later, much to their coworkers' dismay.",
      "category": "entertainment",
