      "id": "012",
      "headline": "Farmer Norm Storm Warns That Corn Born in a Thorn Worn by a Fawn Is Forlorn",
      "summary": "The agricultural community is struggling to parse this prophecy.",
      "fullBody": "Norm Storm, a fourth-generation farmer known for his cryptic weather predictions, has issued a warning so linguistically dense that the USDA has assigned a team of linguists to decode it. 'Corn born in a thorn worn by a fawn is forlorn,' Storm repeated, pointing at a withered stalk. Some interpret it as a warning about invasive species; others believe it's a commentary on fast fashion in the animal kingdom. Either way, local corn futures have plummeted, and a deer named Fawn has been placed in protective custody. 'I'm just saying what the soil told me,' Storm shrugged.",
      "category": "agriculture",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-07-06/012.jpg",
