      "id": "015",
      "headline": "Detective Kent Trent Solves Case of Bent Cent Spent on Scent in a Tent",
      "summary": "The mystery was so convoluted that three writers quit trying to cover it.",
      "fullBody": "Private investigator Kent Trent has cracked what local police are calling 'the most unnecessarily rhyming crime in history.' The case involved a bent penny, a suspicious perfume purchase, and a tent at a music festival. 'It was a scent well spent in a tent,' Trent explained, holding the damaged coin with tweezers. The culprit, a perfumer named Vent who lived in a tent, had been counterfeiting scents. 'I just wanted to make people smell like success,' Vent wept during the arrest. Trent was awarded a plaque and a lifetime supply of breath mints.",
