      "id": "016",
      "headline": "Clown Brown Crown Drowns in Town Gown While Frowning at a Downed Hound",
      "summary": "The incident was tragic yet grammatically impressive; the hound is fine.",
      "fullBody": "Barnaby 'Brown Crown' Clown, a street performer known for his oversized headwear, accidentally fell into a fountain while performing at the Town Gown festival. 'He was frowning at a dog that had fallen down,' explained witness Lynn Finn. 'Then he went down too. It was a whole lot of down.' The hound, a basset named Hound, was unharmed and reportedly enjoyed the splash. Crown was rescued by paramedics and is recovering at St. Frown Hospital. He has vowed to switch to lighter headwear and 'only smile at dogs from now on.'",
