      "id": "017",
      "headline": "Writer Wright Knight Fights for Right to Write Light Plight at Night",
      "summary": "The literary community is split; some call it a bright fight, others a fright.",
      "fullBody": "Novelist Wright Knight has petitioned the Writers' Guild for the right to exclusively write about 'light plights'—minor inconveniences occurring after dark. 'Someone needs to chronicle the tragedy of stubbing your toe at 2 AM,' Knight argued, brandishing a 900-page manuscript titled 'The Night Light Fright.' The guild is divided: traditionalists want to preserve the right to write about heavy plights, while millennials support Knight's 'relatable content.' A compromise may allow 'medium plights' during twilight hours. Knight plans to appeal, claiming the decision is 'not quite right.'",
      "category": "arts",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-07-06/017.jpg",
