      "headline": "Chef Shep Pepp Opens Repp Step, a Restaurant Where You Prep Peppers in a Pep Step",
      "summary": "Diners must chop their own vegetables; the concept is surprisingly popular.",
      "fullBody": "Shep Pepp, a culinary innovator with a lisp and a dream, has opened Repp Step, a farm-to-table restaurant where patrons prepare their own peppers in a choreographed 'Pep Step' routine. 'Food tastes better when you sweat for it,' Pepp said, demonstrating the three-step pepper chop. Customers, wearing custom aprons, dance-chop jalapeños to a beat while Pepp raps about vitamin C. The restaurant has a three-month waitlist, though the ER next door has also seen increased traffic. 'Worth it,' said diner Deb Webb, clutching an ice pack. 'The salsa was transcendent.'",
