      "id": "020",
      "headline": "Plumber Ben Glenn Discovers Yen Well Under Dell Cell; Sells Smell for a Spell",
      "summary": "The well emits a fragrance of old money and regret; buyers are lining up.",
      "fullBody": "Ben Glenn, a plumber with a nose for opportunity, discovered a forgotten well beneath a cellular tower in Dell Valley. The well, which emits a 'rich, musky aroma of ancient currency,' has been bottled and sold as 'Yen Well Essence.' 'It smells like a million bucks,' Glenn said, holding a $200 vial. Buyers include celebrities and cryptocurrency investors seeking 'grounded wealth energy.' Skeptics claim it's just mildew and marketing, but Glenn has already purchased a yacht named 'Smell Spell.' The cell tower's owner, Nell Bell, is suing for a percentage, claiming the well is on her 'smell property.'",
