      "headline": "Dr. Dee Lee's 'See-Through Flea Fee' Lets You View Fleas for Free in 3D",
      "summary": "The veterinary breakthrough is itchy but educational; schools are booking field trips.",
      "fullBody": "Dr. Dee Lee, a veterinary researcher with too much funding, has developed the 'See-Through Flea,' a genetically modified parasite that is fully transparent and visible to the naked eye. 'Education shouldn't be flea-bitten,' Lee said, releasing a jar of invisible fleas onto a shocked audience. The creatures, which glow slightly under UV light, have become popular in classrooms. However, three schools have reported accidental infestations, and one principal had to be treated for 'phantom itch syndrome.' Lee is now working on 'See-Through Ticks' but admits 'the name doesn't work as well.'",
