      "id": "023",
      "headline": "Mayor Fay Gray's 'Ray Day' Law Delayed After Gray Jay Sprayed with Gray Clay",
      "summary": "The bird was fine, but the optics were terrible; PR team in disarray.",
      "fullBody": "Mayor Fay Gray's controversial 'Ray Day' initiative suffered a PR setback when a gray jay was accidentally sprayed with gray clay during a promotional photoshoot. 'We were trying to make the bird look more cheerful,' explained spokesperson Jay Clay. The bird, now a statue-like gray, was unharmed but deeply offended, according to ornithologists. Animal rights groups have called the incident 'avian abuse,' while Gray's opponents claim it proves the mayor is 'out of touch with nature and color theory.' The mayor has postponed the law and adopted the clay-covered bird as a pet named 'Clay Jay.'",
