      "id": "024",
      "headline": "Gardener Parker Harker Plants Darker Parker in Marker for a Starker Larker",
      "summary": "The landscaping project is incomprehensible but visually striking; tourists are flocking.",
      "fullBody": "Parker Harker, a landscape artist with a thesaurus addiction, has created a garden installation so linguistically dense that visitors need a guidebook. 'I planted a darker parker in a marker for a starker larker,' Harker explained, gesturing at what appears to be a bush inside a parking space outlined in marker, surrounded by scarecrows. Art critics have called it 'post-semantic horticulture.' The town of Marker, Arkansas, has seen a 400% increase in tourism, mostly from confused English majors. Harker's next project involves a 'sharper carper' in a 'harper tarpaper.' Local officials are pretending to understand.",
