      "id": "025",
      "headline": "Banker Frank Shank's Prank Tank Sank After He Thanked a Rank Crank in a Yank",
      "summary": "The financial instrument was actually a fish tank; regulators are baffled.",
      "fullBody": "Frank Shank, an investment banker with a mischievous streak, created the 'Prank Tank,' a fake investment vehicle that was literally a fish tank filled with rubber ducks. 'I wanted to see if anyone would read the fine print,' Shank admitted, after the tank 'sank' during a presentation. The problem began when he thanked a 'rank crank' (a disgruntled engineer) for 'yanking' the plug, revealing the water-filled tank. Three investors fainted, one laughed so hard he needed oxygen, and the SEC launched an investigation into 'aquatic securities fraud.' Shank has been sentenced to teach financial literacy at a community pool.",
      "category": "business",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-07-06/025.jpg",
