      "id": "026",
      "headline": "Vet Brett Chet's Pet Jet Lets Pets Set Bets on Wet Vets in a Net",
      "summary": "The in-flight gambling service for animals is surprisingly popular among pigeons.",
      "fullBody": "Dr. Brett Chet, a veterinarian with aviation ambitions, has launched 'Pet Jet,' an airline where animals can gamble on which vet will get soaked during in-flight water emergencies. 'Pets deserve entertainment too,' Chet said, while a parrot placed a bet on 'Wet Vet Number Three.' The service, accessible via paw-friendly touchscreens, has been embraced by pigeons, who are 'natural gamblers,' according to ornithologist Dr. Lett Mett. The FAA is reviewing whether animals can legally place bets, but Chet argues it's 'just pecking on glass, not gambling.' A class-action lawsuit has been filed by a goldfish who claims the water odds were 'fishy.'",
      "category": "animals",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-07-06/026.jpg",
