    {
      "id": "027",
      "headline": "Painter Painter Fainter Paints Painter Fainter in a Tainter; Result is Tainter",
      "summary": "The meta-art piece caused the artist to faint; critics call it 'peak performance art.'",
      "fullBody": "Pat Painter, who legally changed their name to 'Painter Fainter,' has created a self-portrait while sitting in a tainter gate (a type of dam structure) that is so meta it caused the artist to faint. 'I painted a painter fainter in a tainter,' Fainter explained from a hospital bed. 'The tainter made me tainter, and I fainted.' The piece, which is literally just a photo of Fainter unconscious in a dam, sold for $300,000 to a collector who 'appreciates recursive art.' The local water authority is less pleased, billing Fainter $5,000 for 'unauthorized use of infrastructure.' Fainter plans to appeal, claiming the gate was 'just asking to be tainted.'",
      "category": "arts",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-07-06/027.jpg",
      "publishedAt": "1 day ago",
      "readTimeSeconds": 101,
      "tags": [
        "Art",
        "Weird",
        "Meta"
      ],
      "isBreaking": false
    },
    {
      "id": "028",
      "headline": "Rapper Clapper Snapper's 'Dapper Wrapper' Rap Traps Lapper in a Napper",
      "summary": "The song is so catchy that listeners literally can't stop clapping; OSHA is involved.",
      "fullBody": "Clarence 'Clapper Snapper' Trapper, a rapper known for onomatopoeic beats, has released 'Dapper Wrapper,' a track so rhythmically infectious that listeners report uncontrollable clapping for hours. 'I just wanted to make people snap,' Snapper said, while his manager applied ice to his own exhausted hands. The song has been banned in three factories after workers couldn't stop clapping near heavy machinery. One listener, Deb Webb, was found asleep in a recliner ('napper') after clapping herself into exhaustion. 'I couldn't stop,' she mumbled, still clapping weakly. Snapper is working on a follow-up, 'Napper Wrapper,' which he promises will be 'less physically demanding.'",
      "category": "entertainment",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-07-06/028.jpg",
      "publishedAt": "1 day ago",
