      "id": "029",
      "headline": "Sailor Taylor Sailor's Hailer Fails to Mail a Pail of Snail Tail to a Rail Jail",
      "summary": "The postal service is investigating; the snails are unharmed but delayed.",
      "fullBody": "Captain Taylor Sailor, a retired naval officer turned eccentric mailman, attempted to ship a pail of preserved snail tails to a model train jail ('rail jail') using a broken fog horn ('hailer') as packaging. 'I thought the horn would protect the pail,' Sailor explained to postal inspectors. The package was intercepted in Kansas, where workers were baffled by the combination of marine equipment and gastropod appendages. The snails, which were not actually alive, are being held as evidence. The intended recipient, Warden Dale Gale of the Rail Jail Miniature Museum, expressed disappointment: 'I needed those tails for the prisoners' rations.' Sailor has been banned from all USPS facilities and three maritime museums.",
      "category": "local",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-07-06/029.jpg",
