      "id": "030",
      "headline": "Baker Quaker Staker's 'Shaker Maker' Bakes a Faker Taker into a Raker",
      "summary": "The bread was so realistic that a thief tried to steal it; the rake was unimpressed.",
      "fullBody": "Quincy 'Quaker Staker' Baker, a religious baker with a vendetta against thieves, has created the 'Shaker Maker,' a bread oven that bakes loaves shaped like valuable items. 'I baked a faker taker into a raker,' Baker explained, showing a sourdough sculpture of a burglar holding a rake. The piece was so realistic that an actual thief attempted to steal it, only to be raked by the actual rake that Baker had hidden inside. 'The raker raked the faker,' Baker chuckled, while police filled out reports in confused silence. The thief is recovering from minor rake wounds and has been charged with 'attempted gluten theft.' Baker is now working on a 'Caker' that looks like a lawyer.",
      "category": "food",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-07-06/030.jpg",
