      "id": "031",
      "headline": "Dr. Drew Blue's 'True Glue' Sticks Two Shoe Crews into a Stew of Dew",
      "summary": "The adhesive is so strong it accidentally fused two rival dance troupes; they're now one super-troupe.",
      "fullBody": "Dr. Drew Blue, a chemist with a penchant for puns, has invented 'True Glue,' an adhesive so powerful it can bond anything. During a demonstration, two rival 'shoe crews' (tap dance troupes) got stuck together in a puddle of morning dew that had been treated with the glue. 'We were just doing a stew of dew,' Blue explained, as 40 dancers hopped in unison toward a single dressing room. Rather than separate, the crews have embraced their fusion, creating a new style called 'stuck-step.' They're now touring as 'The True Glue Crew' and have a residency in Las Vegas. Blue is being sued by both original troupes but claims 'they're bonded for life now.'",
      "category": "science",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-07-06/031.jpg",
