      "id": "032",
      "headline": "Miner Miner Einer Finds Finer Diner in a Liner Under a Shiner",
      "summary": "The underground restaurant serves only canned goods; critics are surprisingly kind.",
      "fullBody": "Ernest 'Miner Miner' Einer, a coal miner with culinary dreams, discovered a vintage dining car ('liner') buried 200 feet underground while chasing a shiny rock ('shiner'). 'I found a finer diner in a liner,' Einer announced, covered in coal dust and excitement. The car, which serves as a restaurant, offers only canned goods because 'that's what survived the burial.' Despite the limited menu, food critics have praised the 'earthy ambiance' and 'unbeatable isolation.' Reservations are booked through 2028. Einer is now searching for a 'shiner winery' to complete the experience. OSHA has expressed concern but admits 'the reviews are glowing.'",
