      "id": "033",
      "headline": "Fisher Fisher Dishwasher Catches a Wish-Wash in a Swish-Squash",
      "summary": "The fish was so confused it granted three wishes; two were wasted on soap.",
      "fullBody": "Fisher Fisher, a commercial fisherman who moonlights as a dishwasher, claims to have caught a 'wish-wash'—a magical fish that grants wishes but only in the context of cleaning. 'I was washing dishes when I swished a squash and caught it,' Fisher explained, holding a very normal-looking trout. The fish allegedly granted three wishes: Fisher's first two were 'unlimited soap' and 'a sponge that never smells.' By the third wish, he realized his mistake and asked for 'a better understanding of wish economics.' The fish disappeared in a bubble of suds. Fisher is now writing a book, 'Wish-Wash: A Cautionary Tale,' and his dishes have never been cleaner.",
      "category": "local",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-07-06/033.jpg",
