      "id": "035",
      "headline": "Judge Smudge Grudge Nudges a Fudge Budge in a Trudge; Pledge Sludge",
      "summary": "The legal ruling was messy but binding; the courtroom needs new carpet.",
      "fullBody": "Judge Morton 'Smudge' Grudge, known for his messy desk and grumpy demeanor, nudged a 'fudge budge' (a budget made of chocolate) during a long trial trudge, causing a 'pledge sludge' (a funding promise to melt). 'I nudged the budge and the pledge became sludge,' Grudge admitted, wiping chocolate from his gavel. The defendant, a candy manufacturer accused of tax evasion, was found guilty when the fudge budget revealed hidden accounts. The courtroom carpet, however, was declared a total loss. 'Justice is sweet but sticky,' Grudge ruled, sentencing the defendant to 200 hours of community service cleaning municipal buildings.",
      "category": "crime",
