      "id": "036",
      "headline": "Hiker Biker Hiker-Biker Liker Striker Pikes a Dyke on a Trike to a Mike",
      "summary": "The journey was unnecessary; the microphone was only 10 feet away.",
      "fullBody": "Hiram 'Hiker-Biker' Liker, an enthusiast of both walking and cycling, decided to address a town meeting by riding a trike over a small dyke to reach a microphone ('Mike') that was already within walking distance. 'I like to make an entrance,' Liker explained, after crashing into the podium. The trike, which Liker had piked (modified) with hiking boots instead of wheels, was not designed for dykes. The microphone was unharmed, but Liker suffered a bruised ego and a bent pedal. The town council has since banned 'unnecessary vehicular entrances' and installed a sign: 'Mike is 10 feet away. Walk.'",
      "category": "local",
