      "id": "037",
      "headline": "Grocer Kroger's 'Stroker Broker' Smoker Joker Pokes a Poker in a Coker",
      "summary": "The tobacco-themed stock trading game is surprisingly addictive; the SEC is concerned.",
      "fullBody": "Gerald Grocer, who bought a Kroger franchise as a joke, has created 'Stroker Broker,' a board game where players trade stocks while smoking and telling jokes. 'The smoker joker pokes a poker in a coker,' Grocer explained, demonstrating the game's bizarre mechanics. Players must smoke a cigar, tell a joke, and poke a poker chip into a coke oven-shaped board piece to make trades. The game has sold 50,000 copies, mostly to finance bros with irony poisoning. The SEC has launched an investigation into whether 'Stroker Broker' constitutes unlicensed securities trading. Grocer's defense: 'It's just a game, folks. The smoke is optional.' (It is not optional.)",
      "category": "business",
