      "id": "038",
      "headline": "Tailor Taylor's 'Sailer Mailer' Fails to Hail a Pailer in a Jailer's Jail",
      "summary": "The clothing delivery service for prisoners used boats; it was poorly planned.",
      "fullBody": "Taylor Tailor, a seamstress with a nautical obsession, launched 'Sailer Mailer,' a service delivering custom prison uniforms via small sailboats. 'I thought prisoners deserved fashion and fresh air,' Tailor explained, as her fourth boat was intercepted by coast guard. The service failed to 'hail a pailer' (attract a bucket-carrying dock worker) at the 'jailer's jail,' resulting in three escaped boats and one very confused manatee. The uniforms, made of waterproof canvas, are now popular among actual sailors. Tailor has pivoted to 'Sailer Tailor,' a maritime clothing line, and has promised to 'never jail-mail again.'",
      "category": "business",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-07-06/038.jpg",
