      "id": "040",
      "headline": "Carpenter Harper's 'Sharper Carper' Harps on a Parper in a Draper Paper",
      "summary": "The woodworking critic reviews curtains; the drapery industry is in turmoil.",
      "fullBody": "Harriet Harper, a carpenter who moonlights as a 'sharper carper' (harsh critic), has published a scathing review of drapery in the Draper Paper, a textile industry newsletter. 'I harp on a parper in a draper paper,' Harper explained, confusing everyone. The review, which compares curtain rods to 'unfulfilled wooden dreams,' has caused a 15% drop in drapery sales. The Draper Paper's editor, Perry Draper, has begged Harper to stick to furniture. 'She called our best valance 'a fabric lie,' Draper wept. Harper is unrepentant: 'Wood is truth. Fabric is just wood that gave up.' She is currently being sued for 'defamation of drapes.'",
      "category": "arts",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-07-06/040.jpg",
