      "id": "041",
      "headline": "Diver River Shiver's Liver Quiver Delivers a Fiver to a Hiver in a Viver",
      "summary": "The underwater beekeeper paid a hive-dweller; the transaction was damp.",
      "fullBody": "Diana 'River Shiver' Diver, an underwater beekeeper (she keeps bees on floating hives), delivered a five-dollar bill ('fiver') to a 'hiver' (beekeeper) in a 'viver' (a type of basket). 'My liver quivered when I saw the bees,' Diver admitted, though she insists the transaction was professional. The bees, confused by the damp currency, have begun constructing a honeycomb around the fiver. 'They're making money honey,' the hiver reported. Marine biologists are baffled by the combination of aquatics and apiculture. Diver plans to expand her business to 'river liver delivery'—floating meat markets for pescatarians.",
      "category": "agriculture",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-07-06/041.jpg",
