    {
      "id": "043",
      "headline": "Boxer Knox's 'Ox Pox' Jox on a Fox in a Lox; Socks in a Cocks' Flocks",
      "summary": "The chicken-themed boxing match was a fowl affair; the fox was the referee.",
      "fullBody": "Knox Boxer, a pugilist with a poultry obsession, staged 'Ox Pox Jox'—a boxing match where fighters wear ox masks and the ring is surrounded by chickens ('cocks' flocks'). The referee, a man in a fox costume named Fox Lox, declared the match a draw after both boxers were distracted by the chickens. 'I jox on a fox in a lox,' Boxer explained, which means nothing. The event, held in a smokehouse ('lox'), raised $10,000 for chicken literacy. 'Chickens deserve to read,' Boxer insisted, while a rooster pecked at his championship belt. The boxing commission has banned 'animal-themed matches' but praised the 'socks in a cocks' flocks' fashion line.",
      "category": "sports",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-07-06/043.jpg",
      "publishedAt": "1 day ago",
      "readTimeSeconds": 92,
