    {
      "id": "044",
      "headline": "Weaver Beaver's 'Cleaver Fever' Seaver Leaves a Weaver in a Griever's Beaver",
      "summary": "The textile factory's meat-themed break room caused a beaver uprising; grief counselors are on site.",
      "fullBody": "Beatrice 'Beaver' Weaver, who runs a textile factory with a meat-themed break room called 'Cleaver Fever,' accidentally left a 'seaver' (a type of fish knife) in a 'griever's beaver' (a mourning person's hat). 'I seavered the beaver's fever cleaver,' Weaver explained, causing HR to call in grief counselors. The beaver, which is the factory mascot and also a real beaver named Cleaver, became feverish after eating the break room's ham-scented wallpaper. 'He's grieving the loss of his dam-themed break room,' a counselor explained. The factory has returned to standard decor, but Cleaver the Beaver still demands meat-flavored thread. 'Weavers gotta weave,' Weaver sighed, feeding him bacon yarn.",
      "category": "business",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-07-06/044.jpg",
      "publishedAt": "1 day ago",
