      "id": "045",
      "headline": "Ranger Granger's 'Stranger Danger' Manger Changes a Ranger into a Wranger",
      "summary": "The nativity-scene security system works too well; three wise men were detained.",
      "fullBody": "Forest Ranger Greg Granger invented 'Stranger Danger Manger,' a security system for nativity scenes that alerts authorities when unfamiliar figures approach. 'It changes a ranger into a wrangler,' Granger explained, demonstrating how the system lassoed a suspicious shepherd. The system worked too well at the Bethlehem Mall, where it detained three men carrying gifts, a drummer boy, and a confused camel. 'We thought they were stealing the baby Jesus,' Granger admitted, releasing the wise men with gift cards. The camel is still in custody pending identification. Granger has since added a 'wise man whitelist' and a 'no-lasso' setting for livestock.",
      "category": "tech",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-07-06/045.jpg",
      "publishedAt": "1 day ago",
