        "Animals"
      ],
      "isBreaking": false
    },
    {
      "id": "047",
      "headline": "Crier Drier's 'Frier Flier' Trier Dyes a Trier in a Drier; Buyers Cry a Liar",
      "summary": "The laundry-themed restaurant served dyed clothes; customers expected food.",
      "fullBody": "Craig 'Crier' Drier opened 'Frier Flier,' a restaurant that serves only fried fliers (leaflets) and dyes clothes in the dryers. 'I trier dyes a trier in a drier,' Drier explained, which is his business model. Customers, expecting food, were instead given tie-dyed laundry and crispy paper. 'He cried he was a fryer, but he's just a drier liar,' complained buyer Mya Fryer. The health department shut down the establishment, but not before Drier sold 200 'vintage dyed tees' to confused hipsters. 'I thought it was ironic,' said one customer, wearing a shirt dyed in ketchup. Drier is planning a 'Crier Drier' laundromat where employees weep while folding.",
      "category": "food",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-07-06/047.jpg",
      "publishedAt": "1 day ago",
      "readTimeSeconds": 94,
