    },
    {
      "id": "048",
      "headline": "Skier's Sneer at a Freer Queer in a Beer Pier; Leer Seers Steer Clear of a Sheer Sphere",
      "summary": "The ski resort's LGBTQ+ beer garden was so popular it became a tourist attraction; geometry enthusiasts are confused.",
      "fullBody": "A skier's sneer at a 'freer queer' (budget-friendly LGBTQ+ patron) in a 'beer pier' (floating bar) at Alpine Queer Resort caused 'leer seers' (judgmental onlookers) to steer clear of a 'sheer sphere' (transparent disco ball). 'The sheer sphere made the seers steer clear of the queer beer pier,' explained resort owner Mx. Sheer. The sneering skier was actually sneering at the cold, not the patrons, but the misunderstanding made the resort a viral sensation. The sheer sphere has been named an official landmark. 'Geometry is gay culture now,' Sheer declared, while mathematicians protested the 'inaccurate use of sheer.' The skier has apologized and opened a 'Sneer-Free Queer Beer Pier' franchise.",
      "category": "lifestyle",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-07-06/048.jpg",
      "publishedAt": "1 day ago",
      "readTimeSeconds": 96,
      "tags": [
