        "Travel"
      ],
      "isBreaking": false
    },
    {
      "id": "049",
      "headline": "Mason Dason's 'Bason Rason' Season Reason Treason in a Gason's Eason",
      "summary": "The bricklayer's podcast about soup-related betrayals has 2 million subscribers; no one understands why.",
      "fullBody": "Mason Dason, a bricklayer with a microphone, hosts 'Bason Rason,' a podcast investigating 'season reason treason' in the soup industry. 'I season the reason for the treason in a gason's eason,' Dason explains every episode, referring to gas station soup season. The podcast, which accuses Campbell's of 'broth betrayal,' has 2 million subscribers who 'don't really get it but can't stop listening.' Dason's evidence includes a 1987 memo about reducing noodle counts. 'That's treason,' Dason insists, while soup historians point out that 'gason' isn't a word. The podcast has been optioned for a Netflix series starring a soup can.",
      "category": "entertainment",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-07-06/049.jpg",
      "publishedAt": "1 day ago",
      "readTimeSeconds": 88,
      "tags": [
